+# Historical Step 5.8 aggregation transition
+
+This opt-in owner record is limited to the first paused, drained Step 5.9 repair wave, before its native pack or collection exists. Ordinary runs and sibling-contract history retain their existing checks.
+
+The prior immutable certificate and genuine successful tool result retain their original bytes. An actual pre-battery preparation pins the old merged-cache hash. The actual engine battery event chain authenticates a successful native merge after that certification. Exact archived before/current copies of all 81 batch contracts reproduce the native-after and owner-after merged caches byte for byte using the ordinary merger's ordering and serialization. The owner's application, approved literal operations, frozen frontier, full source vector, and creation state/request are bound by raw hashes.
+
+The original cache preimage may be unavailable. In that case the record authenticates only its historical certificate reference and the genuine subsequent derived-cache transition; it never claims those missing bytes were recovered or that the old cache can be reconstructed. This reference is used only by `verifyEvidence`. It is **not** a supporting-metadata archive and cannot satisfy `frozenSupportingEvidence`'s exact-preimage requirement.
+
+The application may contain individually guarded boundary reviews, risk-review/citation-use fields, and one separately declared draft scientific repair with its own contract, source mirror, and consumer quote. Replaying the literal operations must account for every metadata difference; every other source byte remains exact. Source repair and all transitive in-scope consumers become mandatory genuine current native gate-review targets, assigned together in dependency order. A completed collection missing any of those reviews fails. Existing context checks still reject stale source/supplier contexts, and ordinary interface propagation and same-reviewer duties remain active. No history entry supplies review, audit, Sol, threshold, creation, or mathematical acceptance credit.
+
+`recordGateAggregationHistory(root, run, payload)` validates the actual paused/drained boundary and exact current inputs, supplies its truthful recording time, and writes the immutable `gate-1-owner-aggregation-history.json` marker. There is no overwrite mode. Later verification reads the archived transition, so ordinary later repairs do not falsify historical source observations. New certification separately pins the actual current merged-cache bytes at an absolute path; the original relative cache pin remains a historical declaration. An arbitrary edit to that fresh current pin still fails verification.
+
+Prepare the payload with the run-owned `prepare-request.mjs` after the controller is stopped or held at the intended recording boundary. It only archives current state/request and emits a proposed payload; it does not activate history or run a gate. Invoke the exported recorder only after code review and installation. Then perform ordinary fresh preparation, owner recertification, native gate-owner reviews, certification, and the full battery. Original certificates, reports, failed gate events, and collection artifacts are never rewritten.
